{
  "x-call": "wingtip_route::motion::call",
  "description": "A recorded flight made ready (replay_track) made ready for a flight simulator's replay: each run of reports between two gaps its own segment, nothing drawn across a gap; the path between reports a cubic Hermite spline through each report with its sent velocity as the slope (de Boor 1978, ch. IV), the height the same with the vertical speed, `rate_hz` frames a second (10 where not given, at most 60); pressure altitude set on the airplane's own altimeter setting where it sent one below 18,000 ft (14 CFR 91.121(a)(1); FAA-H-8083-25C ch. 11), else left as sent and the segment's `msl` false; on the ground, the ground's height. Estimated, as ADS-B sends none of them: bank from the turn, tan(bank) = V x turn rate / g (FAA-H-8083-25C ch. 5), pitch the flight path angle, each and the heading averaged over 2.5 s each side so the airplane rolls in before the heading moves (FAA-H-8083-15B ch. 7, a lead of half the bank); heading the track (no wind known), and magnetic by the WMM; gear and flaps by phase (FAA-H-8083-3C ch. 6, retracted once climbing; down below 1,000 ft above the ground descending, AC 120-108); lights by AIM 4-3-24 and 14 CFR 91.209.",
